  "id": "fuzzy-set-theory",
  "term": "fuzzy set theory",
  "definition": "Fuzzy set theory is an approach for representing data in a way that captures ambiguity and uncertainty rather than treating values as completely fixed. In the source material, it is used to turn image grayscale levels into fuzzy sets so uncertain visual information can be modeled more robustly and compared before and after enhancement.",
